# citehop

This project builds a **local, resumable 1-hop citation corpus around any seed paper** (the paper + papers it cites + papers that cite it). QC4HEP / Di Meglio 2024 is only `--preset qc4hep`.

- Input is a seed (`--doi`, `--arxiv`, `--title --author`, or `--preset`), not a hardcoded paper.
- Live APIs only (arXiv, Crossref, Semantic Scholar, OpenAlex, Unpaywall). No remembered paper text.
- Do not expand to 2-hop unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not scrape paywalls. Metadata + abstract if there is no OA copy.
- Each seed writes to `~/Library/Metadata/<slug>/`. Re-runs resume via `manifest.db`.
- Do not write corpora under `~/opt/citehop`. That tree is application code only.
- After the user confirms a sample, full build is `python -m citehop build --yes ...`.
